# EALHO THERAPY — CURSOR RULES
# Read this entire file before writing any code.
# This file is for the Ealho Therapy project ONLY.

---

## 1. WHO YOU ARE BUILDING FOR

Ealho Therapy (ealhohq.com)
- AI-powered therapy booking and session platform for Nigerian patients and therapists
- Patients book sessions with or without an account
- Therapists manage availability, join video sessions, review AI-generated SOAP notes
- Mobile-first: all patient-facing screens designed at 375px width first
- Primary users are on mobile, Nigerian network conditions, mid-range Android devices
- WhatsApp is the primary notification channel — more important than email for Nigerian users

This is NOT Ealho Notes AI.
Do not build API key management, enterprise dashboards, AssemblyAI, Recall.ai,
FHIR output, Stripe billing, or organization hierarchies in this project.

---

## 2. TECH STACK — NEVER DEVIATE FROM THIS

Frontend
- Framework: Next.js 14 with App Router — always App Router, never Pages Router
- Language: TypeScript — always, no plain JavaScript files ever
- Styling: Tailwind CSS — utility classes only, no CSS modules, no styled-components
- UI Components: shadcn/ui — use existing components before building custom ones
- Animations: Framer Motion — for transitions and mobile micro-interactions
- Forms: React Hook Form + Zod — always validate with Zod schemas
- State: Zustand — global state only, use React state for local component state
- Data Fetching: TanStack Query — for all server state, loading states, and caching

Backend
- Framework: FastAPI (Python) — async endpoints only, always use async def
- Background Jobs: Celery + Redis — all async tasks (note generation, PDF export)
- PDF Generation: WeasyPrint — always queue via Celery, store in Supabase Storage, return signed URL
- AI Notes: Claude API primary (claude-sonnet-4-20250514), DeepSeek fallback
- DB Client in FastAPI: Supabase Python client — never SQLAlchemy

Database
- Database: Supabase (Postgres)
- ORM: Prisma — all schema changes via Prisma schema file only
- Migrations: Prisma Migrate — npx prisma migrate dev always, never manual SQL schema changes
- Caching and Slot Locking: Upstash Redis
- Security: Supabase RLS — every table must have RLS policies

Database Schema Separation
supabase/
├── schemas/
│   ├── therapy/    # patients, bookings, sessions, availability, therapists
│   └── shared/     # profiles, subscriptions

Auth
- Provider: Supabase Auth — never build custom auth from scratch
- Route Protection: Next.js Middleware — always check role in middleware first
- Roles: patient, therapist, admin
- Role Storage: custom claims in JWT via Supabase app_metadata — never store role only on frontend
- Guest Booking: signed one-time JWT tokens — no Supabase session required
- Therapist Status: separate from role — pending / approved / rejected / suspended
- Token Storage: HttpOnly cookies only — never localStorage, never sessionStorage
- One login page at /login for all roles — role determines redirect after login

Login Routes
/login              → one page, all roles log in here
/signup             → patient self-registration
/therapist/enroll   → therapist application (separate multi-step form)
/admin/login        → admin only, not linked publicly

Role Redirects After Login
patient   → /dashboard
therapist → /therapist/dashboard
admin     → /admin/dashboard

Video and Communication
- Video: Agora Web SDK — no Daily.co, no Zoom SDK, no Google Meet ever
- Transcription: Agora native transcription — no Whisper, no separate recording tool
- Email: Resend — all transactional emails
- WhatsApp: WhatsApp Business API — primary notification channel

Payments
- Paystack only — NGN payments
- Never use Stripe in this project
- Use Paystack modal for checkout — never build custom payment UI
- Slot locking: Upstash Redis with 10-minute TTL during Paystack checkout

Hosting
- Frontend: Netlify — auto-deploy from GitHub
- Backend: DigitalOcean App Platform — $12/mo basic tier
- Never suggest Vercel, Railway, or Render

Error Tracking
- Sentry — wrap all API routes and critical functions

