## 4. AUTHENTICATION RULES

Golden Rules
1. Role lives in JWT app_metadata — never trust role from request body
2. Always check role in middleware BEFORE rendering any page
3. Always enforce RLS at database level — frontend checks are UI only
4. Always check therapist status = approved separately from role = therapist
5. Never store JWT in localStorage — HttpOnly cookies only
6. Guest bookings have zero auth — public endpoints only
7. Guest session access via signed one-time token in URL — expires at session end time

Middleware Pattern
export async function middleware(req: NextRequest) {
  const supabase = createMiddlewareClient({ req, res })
  const { data: { session } } = await supabase.auth.getSession()
  const role = session?.user?.app_metadata?.role
  const status = session?.user?.app_metadata?.status
  const path = req.nextUrl.pathname

  if (!session && isProtectedPath(path)) {
    return NextResponse.redirect(new URL('/login', req.url))
  }
  if (role === 'therapist' && status === 'pending' && path.startsWith('/therapist/dashboard')) {
    return NextResponse.redirect(new URL('/therapist/pending', req.url))
  }
  if (role === 'patient' && path.startsWith('/therapist')) {
    return NextResponse.redirect(new URL('/dashboard', req.url))
  }
  if (role === 'therapist' && path.startsWith('/admin')) {
    return NextResponse.redirect(new URL('/therapist/dashboard', req.url))
  }
}

---

## 5. DATABASE RULES

Prisma Rules
- Always define all models in prisma/schema.prisma
- Never write raw SQL for schema changes
- Always run npx prisma migrate dev after schema changes
- Always run npx prisma generate after schema changes
- Use @db.Uuid for all ID fields
- Use @default(now()) for createdAt and updatedAt

Key Tables
therapy.patients
therapy.therapists              with status: pending/approved/rejected/suspended
therapy.bookings                supports both guest and registered patients
therapy.sessions
therapy.session_notes           SOAP notes — therapist access only via RLS
therapy.availability_schedule   weekly recurring schedule
therapy.availability_overrides  date-specific overrides
therapy.credits
shared.profiles                 extends Supabase auth.users

RLS Rules
- Every table must have RLS enabled — no exceptions
- Therapists read and write own sessions and notes only
- Patients read and write own bookings and profile only
- Admins have full read access, limited write access
- SOAP notes: therapist-only — patients have zero access under any circumstance

---

## 6. AVAILABILITY SYSTEM RULES

- All times stored and displayed in WAT (West Africa Time, UTC+1)
- Slot locking: Upstash Redis with 10-minute TTL during Paystack checkout
- Never double-book: check Redis lock AND database before confirming slot
- Slot generation: start_time + (session_duration + buffer) * n until end_time
- Always check availability_overrides before availability_schedule
- Booking window: default 4 weeks maximum
- Minimum notice: default 2 hours before session
- Never use Google Calendar API — built-in system only
- Never use Cal.com — built-in system only

---

## 7. SOAP NOTE GENERATION RULES

Model Priority
async def generate_note(transcript, session_data, specialty="therapy", note_type="soap"):
    try:
        return await generate_with_claude(transcript, template, session_data)
    except Exception as e:
        log_to_sentry(e, level="warning")
        try:
            result = await generate_with_deepseek(transcript, template, session_data)
            result["_generated_by"] = "deepseek"
            return result
        except Exception as e2:
            log_to_sentry(e2, level="error")
            raise HTTPException(status_code=503, detail="Note generation unavailable")

Claude Rules
- Always use claude-sonnet-4-20250514 — never change the model
- max_tokens: 4000 for intake assessment, 2000 for SOAP note
- Always parse response as JSON — validate against Pydantic schema before saving
- Always instruct Claude: use client_id or initials only — never full patient name
- Always instruct Claude: write "Not reported" for missing info — never invent
- Always require risk assessment section — never omit
- Delete transcript immediately after note generation is confirmed saved

DeepSeek Rules
- Use OpenAI-compatible client with DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL
- Use identical prompt template as Claude — output schema must be identical
- Use response_format json_object always
- Never expose to user which model generated the note

Specialty Template System
TEMPLATES = {
    "therapy": {
        "intake": load_prompt("therapy_intake.txt"),
        "soap": load_prompt("therapy_soap.txt"),
    },
}

---

## 8. MOBILE-FIRST RULES

- Design and build all patient-facing components at 375px first
- Minimum tap target size: 48x48px — no exceptions
- Bottom navigation bar on mobile for patient dashboard
- Agora video call: full-screen, minimal UI, end call button at bottom center
- Paystack: use their modal — never build custom payment UI
- WhatsApp notifications: always implement alongside email — WhatsApp is primary
- Use next/image for all images — never raw img tags
- All images must have explicit width and height to prevent layout shift
- Single column layouts on mobile — never side-by-side on 375px

---

## 9. API RULES

- Always use async def for all route handlers
- Always use Pydantic models for request and response validation
- Always return consistent response structure:
{
  "success": True,
  "data": {},
  "error": None,
  "meta": { "timestamp": "..." }
}
- Always handle errors with try/except
- Always log errors to Sentry
- Never return raw database errors to the client

